*Run visualization on a SAVED preprocessed bundle (Code Civil, qid=192)*

1. Go to the folder:

cd "<repo>\RQ2_Structure_Aware_Retrieval\RQ2_T08_RAG_VISUALIZATION"


2. Activate T08's venv:

Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned

.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1


3. Launch the viewer pointed at the preprocessed bundle:

.\.venv\Scripts\streamlit.exe run src\visualization\app.py -- `
  --bundle-json="..\RQ2_T03_ARM1_NAIVE\data\1804_03_21_1804032150\t08_bundles\483beb56a47b\q192.json" `
  --db="$env:RQ2_BSARD_DB" `
  --mode=retrieval --arm=arm1


Notes:
- The bundle ships its own raw_text + article_spans, so the viewer does NOT
  re-chunk or re-locate articles — it renders the preprocessed top-200 pool
  (method=arm1_pool) for qid=192 directly.
- --db is only used to populate the article-text expanders / GT panel labels;
  retrieval itself is fully offline against the bundle.
- GT bsard_ids: [920, 1014, 1045] (Art. 32 / 146bis / 193ter, Code Civil).
  Expected: 10 correctly-retrieved chunks (green ✓) and 190 wrongly-retrieved
  chunks (red ✗) in the top-200 pool.


